Enemies may lose nerve when their original leader or first caster/healer
falls, half their original group dies, or their last fighter has 25% health
or less. Each trigger checks once; simultaneous triggers share one roll.

                    Hold   Yield   Flee
  Steadfast          85%     10%     5%
  Wary               65%     25%    10%
  Craven             40%     40%    20%
  Skittish beast     65%      0%    35%

Undead, constructs, some bosses, and foes without a breaking temperament
never break. Practice foes and companions do not surrender.
A surrendered enemy stands aside: nobody attacks it and it attacks nobody.
A fleeing enemy leaves this encounter and gives no experience or loot.

Company nerve checks once when at least half your starting company falls
or the surviving members have at most 25% of their combined maximum health.
You never roll. Companions below 25 loyalty have a 20% chance to hesitate
and a 5% chance to flee. With loyalty 25 or higher but chemistry below
Familiar, they have a 10% chance to hesitate and never flee.
Hesitation costs one action and does not add a lost action to a blocking
status. A cancelled companion chant returns half its mana. A fled companion
keeps gear and wounds, returns after settlement wherever you are (even
if you've been moved since), and loses 5 loyalty.
At zero loyalty, the existing desertion rules apply.

Leaving a battle: <ansi fg="command">retreat [exit]</ansi> (or <ansi fg="command">flee</ansi>) prepares for one round,
then attempts to move the company together. See <ansi fg="command">help retreat</ansi>.

See also: help mercy, help chemistry, help alignment, help combat, help separation.
